// Typecheck project for the copy workbench.
//
// The workbench is NOT part of the web app's own tsconfig (`../tsconfig.json`
// includes only src/ + the vite/vitest/storybook/eslint-rules glue), so it needs
// this separate project to be checked at all. It extends the app's compiler
// options so the workbench is held to exactly the same strictness.
//
// WIRED IN, deliberately: `@mythrun/web`'s `typecheck` script runs
// `tsc --noEmit && pnpm copy-workbench:check`, so this project is covered by
// every existing caller of that script — the pre-push frontend gate, CI's
// frontend-check.yml (`pnpm --filter @mythrun/web typecheck`), and the root
// `pnpm typecheck`. Chaining it onto `typecheck` rather than adding a standalone
// step is the point: there is no separate gate anyone can forget to wire up.
//
// This file existed but nothing ran it, so the workbench silently rotted through
// several rounds of contract changes (RollCardLabels, CharacterSheetRevealProps,
// PartyRosterProps, the billing grant ledger, CreditBalance's explainers) while
// every sweep stayed green. The workbench is the surface Miklos reviews copy in —
// a broken one blocks the copy pass — so it gets a real gate.
{
  "extends": "../tsconfig.json",
  "include": ["**/*.ts", "**/*.tsx"],
  "exclude": ["dist"]
}
